# Exercise: Worker Pool
#
# Multiple workers processing from the same pair of channels:
# one for work items, one for results. Each worker captures
# both channels via closure (no `2dup` needed — same rule as
# every spawn so far).
#
# Workers naturally load-balance: whichever worker calls
# `chan.receive` first grabs the next work item.
#
# Your task: spawn two workers (each adds 1 to a value), send
# 10 and 20 as work items, receive both results, sum them.
# Expected: 11 + 21 = 32.
#
# When done, delete the marker line below.

# I AM NOT DONE

: test-worker-pool ( -- )
    chan.make           # ( work )
    chan.make           # ( work results )

    # Spawn two workers — closure captures work + results from the stack
    [ over chan.receive drop 1 i.+ swap chan.send drop drop ] strand.spawn drop
    [ over chan.receive drop 1 i.+ swap chan.send drop drop ] strand.spawn drop
    # Stack still ( work results )

    # Send two work items
    over 10 swap chan.send drop
    over 20 swap chan.send drop

    # Your code here — receive both results, sum them, drop the
    # leftover work and results channels so only the sum remains.
    drop drop 0
    # Do not edit below this line
    # Results are 11 and 21, sum is 32
    32 test.assert-eq
;
